From af64ea55db11c84b0ed4240087c62219d3837232 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:58:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 42/42] tegra_audio: the room noise of the built-in microphone,
 as measured

At +24 dB of boost the room noise measured -33 dBFS, not -36.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/tegra/tegra_audio.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/tegra/tegra_audio.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/tegra/tegra_audio.cpp
index a004635089..071cff51e7 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/tegra/tegra_audio.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/tegra/tegra_audio.cpp
@@ -2197,7 +2197,7 @@ tegra_audio_init_driver(device_node* node, void** _cookie)
 	audio->recordLevel[0] = audio->recordLevel[1] = 11;
 	// The built-in digital microphone only follows the boost (the record
 	// gain is that of the analog path): +24 dB gives speech a good level,
-	// with the room noise around -36 dBFS
+	// with the room noise around -33 dBFS
 	audio->micBoost = 4;
 	audio->inputSource = 0;
 	audio->recordInterruptInstalled = install_io_interrupt_handler(
-- 
2.39.5

